H29 gloss pass A (Opus vision, 28 Sept 2026, prompt scripts/PROMPTS.md "H29 gloss passes"). Rows verbatim. Its warning, verbatim: "four of the 28 crop files are byte-identical duplicates (md5), so four band/segment slots hold another band's crop: L04_s4 = L03_s4, L05_s2 = L04_s2, L06_s4 = L05_s4, L07_s1 = L06_s1 ... in most bands the gloss row is cut off at the top edge. Only the lower halves of the letters show, so nearly every gloss reading below is low confidence ... These crops are not good enough for a blind gloss pass. They should be re-cut about 40-60 px higher, or 300 px tall, so the whole gloss row is inside the frame, and the four duplicate files should be regenerated before any reconciliation." Per-band counts: L01 5, L02 6, L03 11, L04 8, L05 6, L06 7, L07 3.
